                     "topFinding":  "This is the first full Tier-1 + domain fan-out (27 lenses) run against Scheduler since the 2026-07-24 pass only covered part of the lens set, and it surfaced real correctness bugs the lighter pass missed: three separate handlers commit multi-statement D1 writes as unbatched serial calls, so a mid-request interruption can silently truncate a user\u0027s org scope, strand a swapped shift with no assignee, or leave approved time off half-blocked. shift_assignments has no UNIQUE(shift_id, user_id) constraint, so the open-shifts claim path can double-book past max_employees under a race. apps/api runs hono 4.12.18 and apps/web runs react-router-dom 7.15.0, both carrying in-range HIGH CVEs a plain pnpm update would fix. The release pipeline itself got bypassed: commit ffc1e45 (2026-07-31) is titled like a v0.7.1 release but only touched a script, while a real perf fix and migration 0011 sat unreleased at HEAD for 9+ days. Health drops from 85 to 68 and the verdict flips to needs-attention on the strength of these live-breakage findings.",
